PART G – QUALITY AND SAFETY OF ENGINEERING RESULTS

34. Important Engineering Safeguards

- Never fabricate MoRTH or IRC clauses.
- Never use an unverified specification value as a mandatory limit.
- Never assume a universal density, thickness, temperature, gradient, application rate or test frequency.
- Distinguish design values, actual measurements and approved acceptance limits.
- Distinguish calculations from certified engineering approval.
- Require appropriate input data before calculating.
- Show NOT ASSESSED when information is insufficient.
- Preserve the project's approved design and contract requirements.
- Keep all historical calculation records reproducible.
- Provide source references for specification-dependent results.
- Flag outdated standards and unverified criteria.
- Do not replace engineering judgement or approved design verification with automated calculator outputs.

